    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0825" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.52/116b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Third Secretary
                        of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-24T11:00:00-04:00">September 24, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. In view of apparently reliable press reports, you should withdraw from
                    Madrid at once unless some imperative duty compels you to remain. This
                    withdrawal should include Johnson<anchor n="49" xml:id="d744-f1"/> and all
                    American staff. War Department states this withdrawal should also include Col.
                        Fuqua.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d744-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d744-f1" n="49" xml:id="d744-f1-content">
                <p>John D. Johnson, Consul at Madrid.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d744-f2" n="50" xml:id="d744-f2-content">
                <p>Col. Stephen O. Fuqna, Military Attaché in Spain.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
